ng auto-delete rules","description":"Auto-delete rules automatically remove findings from the system based on predefined criteria. These rules help manage the life-cycle of vulnerabilities by ensuring that resolved or outdated findings are removed, reducing clutter and maintaining a clean, up-to-date database. This automation streamlines the vulnerability management process and ensures that teams focus on current and relevant issues.","locale":"en-US","canonical_url":"https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/sem-deleting-stale-findings-automatically.html","release":"australia","topic_type":"concept","last_updated":"2026-03-12","reading_time_minutes":1,"breadcrumb":["Automating prioritization and triaging","Security Exposure Management workflow","Explore","Unified Security Exposure Management","Security Operations"],"tags":["#security-management","#type-concept"]},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"key":"ServiceNowOfficialDocs/security-management/sem-deleting-stale-findings-automatically.md"},
